 "short_name": "Bela-Bela",
 "_doc": "TAX INVOICE/STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT, emunsoft ledger family (same engine as KwaDukuza / Abaqulusi / Alfred Duma). Masthead 'BELA-BELA MUNICIPALITY / PRIVATE BAG X 1609 BELA BELA 0480', VAT No.:4850128515. Fingerprint = masthead AND that VAT number, so it can never match a sibling emunsoft municipality. LAYOUT: header block of 'Label: value' pairs (Account Number / Account Date / Consumer Name / Tax Invoice No. / ERF Description / Suburb / Street / Market Value / Land Area / Deposit / Internet PIN). Then 'METER READINGS' with columns METER NO. / METER TYPE / OLD READING / NEW READING / READING DATE / READING TYPE / CONSUMPTION -- note this variant prints a SINGLE reading date (the new-reading date), a one-letter READING TYPE ('E' -> Estimated via TRANSLATE) and NO 'LEVIED AMOUNT' column. Alfred Duma's variant of the same engine instead prints CONSUMPTION then LEVIED AMOUNT then a date RANGE and no reading type; the two meter-row patterns are therefore not interchangeable. There is exactly ONE electricity meter ([number removed]) on all 10 bills, so the meter row is captured by a single no-collect multi-field rule; the meter rolls over at 1,000,000 (985,731 -> 6,738 on the Jan-2026 bill), so total_kwh is taken from the printed CONSUMPTION column and never from end-minus-start. Then 'ACCOUNT DETAILS' ledger DATE / CODE / DESCRIPTION / UNITS / TARIFF / VALUE where VATable lines carry a '*' marker before the amount. Codes across the 10-bill set: 002004 ENERGY CHARGE (electricity, kWh @ 3.1368 rising to 3.5069 in Jul-2026), 004041 SEWERAGE BASIC CHARGE (sewerage, 1.000 @ 272.00 -> 281.00), 000020 WARNING LETTER ADMIN FEE, 000023 CN/DN FEES (a debit note of 431.00 and its credit-note reversal 431.00-), 008888 DIRECT DEPOSIT PAYMENT, 009008 VAT, 009001 INTEREST. No water and no rates lines on this account. SUMMING CHOICES: electricity has exactly ONE charge line, so standard_kwh / standard_r = the ENERGY CHARGE line (collect:sum so a future mid-period tariff change producing two lines still aggregates) and other_r is '_none' -- the admin fee, CN/DN fees and interest are NOT electricity, they go to the sundry row, and the sewerage basic charge goes to the sewerage row. Flat single-band LV supply: no TOU, no demand, no NMD -> those canonical columns are '_none'. RULE ZERO: the bill prints no independent ex-VAT electricity total, so total_ex_vat_r maps to the SAME printed ENERGY CHARGE amount as standard_r -- the reconcile leg is therefore degenerate (one printed line on both sides) and proves nothing; see the report. The genuine checks are (a) METER READINGS CONSUMPTION == the ENERGY CHARGE units column (two independently printed tables), (b) units x tariff == the printed line value, (c) printed VAT == 15% of the sum of the '*'-marked ledger lines.",
